# Workspace Package Architecture

Every workspace module (CRM, Payroll, Project Management, etc.) is a **separate sibling repo** — never built only inside `urx-workspace-template`.

## Repo layout (required)

```
../urx-<module>-package/          # or ../urx-workspace-<module>/
├── bin/cli.mjs                   # install | sync | uninstall
├── lib/installer.mjs             # copy files + patch host markers
├── package.manifest.json         # nav, collections, modules page, layout, …
├── package.json
├── README.md
└── files/                        # source mirrored under host src/ paths
    └── src/routes/(app)/…
    └── src/lib/…
```

Examples: `urx-crm-package`, `urx-accounting-package`, `urx-project_management-package`, `urx-workspace-payroll`.

## Host template (`urx-workspace-template`)

- **Do not** add module routes, repositories, or UI only in the template.
- Install from the package repo:

```bash
pnpm workspace:<module>:install   # e.g. workspace:project-management:install
pnpm workspace:<module>:sync      # after editing installed files in host
pnpm workspace:<module>:uninstall
```

- Package scripts in host `package.json` point to `../<package-repo>/bin/cli.mjs`.
- Installed files are tracked in `.urx-packages/<package-id>.json`.

## Integration patches (marker comments)

The installer patches **host core files** with `// <package-id>:<area>:start/end` markers:

| Area | Host file |
|------|-----------|
| Nav | `src/lib/navigation/app-nav.ts` |
| Package catalog | `src/lib/shared/workspace-packages.ts` |
| Collections | `src/lib/server/db/collections.ts` |
| App layout nested sections | `src/routes/(app)/+layout.svelte` |
| Modules page | `src/routes/(app)/modules/+page.svelte` |
| Dashboard overview | `src/lib/server/dashboard/build-workspace-overview.ts` |
| Icons | `src/lib/icons/solar-icons.ts`, `register-solar-icons.ts` |
| Module integrations | `src/lib/shared/workspace-module-integrations.ts` |
| Env | `.env.example` |

Define needles/replacements in `package.manifest.json` — copy from an existing package.

## Workflow for a new module

1. Create sibling repo with `files/`, `bin/cli.mjs`, `lib/installer.mjs`, `package.manifest.json`.
2. Add `workspace:<module>:{install,sync,uninstall}` scripts to host `package.json`.
3. Implement module under `files/src/…` (routes, `$lib/server/repositories`, `$lib/shared`, API `/api/v1/<module>/*`).
4. Run `pnpm workspace:<module>:install` from host to apply patches.
5. Update `src/lib/shared/openapi/v1.ts` in the **host** when adding API routes.
6. After host edits, run `pnpm workspace:<module>:sync` to push changes back to the package repo.

## Sample data (seeding) — required for list modules

Modules with explorable records (CRM, Project Management, etc.) must ship **tagged sample data** like CRM:

| Piece | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Seed templates | `$lib/server/<module>/seed-data.ts` |
| Seed repository | `$lib/server/repositories/<module>-seed.ts` |
| Shared types | `$lib/shared/<module>/seed.ts` (`*SeedStatus`, `*_SEED_SUMMARY`) |
| Messages | `$lib/shared/<module>/messages.ts` (load/remove/fail copy) |
| Settings UI | Load + remove buttons, confirm dialog, toasts |
| API | `GET/POST/DELETE /api/v1/<module>/seed` |
| Status API | Include `seedStatus` in `GET /api/v1/<module>/status` |
| Client onboarding | Tokenized invite email + public form route + responses on project detail |
| Documents | Tag inserts with `isSeed: true`; delete only `{ isSeed: true }` |

Reference: `urx-crm-package` (`crm-seed.ts`, `crm-delete-seed-dialog.svelte`, `/api/v1/crm/seed`).

## Do not

- Ship a module only in the template with no package repo.
- Skip `.urx-packages` manifest or install scripts.
- Import `$lib/server/**` or `mongodb` from client-eligible code (see `sveltekit-mongodb-engineering.mdc`).
